ed}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0b197e8d11a6415d81d6b1755946a3ae3f021e1f7909676de2865bdd2b51aa1" "basis" 1438 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/example-4699.json" "file_sha256" "cb0b97387d73b996adebc98edfee72459a458c1cbc5690e11dd0cca32a2549e9" "basis" 1438 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y=1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/example-4699.json" "file_sha256" "cb0b97387d73b996adebc98edfee72459a458c1cbc5690e11dd0cca32a2549e9" "basis" 1438 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=4 \\\\ 4x+10y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/example-4700.json" "file_sha256" "a5d252a64d8aa411380c1727a7cf5c2f290874e8828e3ba001d836d3591d7350" "basis" 1438 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{5}{2}y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/example-4700.json" "file_sha256" "a5d252a64d8aa411380c1727a7cf5c2f290874e8828e3ba001d836d3591d7350" "basis" 1438 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040382/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-20782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=-3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "552d4b9169c04e371eca500ca7fbe5218107176353f77d73bfc1d792861875ab"} {"question" "q-20782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 16 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 16 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "552d4b9169c04e371eca500ca7fbe5218107176353f77d73bfc1d792861875ab"} {"question" "q-20963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20963" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "552d4b9169c04e371eca500ca7fbe5218107176353f77d73bfc1d792861875ab"} {"question" "q-73738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field