_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "552d4b9169c04e371eca500ca7fbe5218107176353f77d73bfc1d792861875ab"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "M∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ 2x+8y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-4y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "552d4b9169c04e371eca500ca7fbe5218107176353f77d73bfc1d792861875ab"} {"question" "q-20783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ -3x+6y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-73750" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value