matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 32 & -40 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & 32 & -40 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 20 & -25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=-5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+4y=-5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-5-4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5-4y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/state.json" "file_sha256" "418a179e8ba02f09c3314aad6634ae507ae2eb1697f0e4e8c62a9668b3f712b0"} {"question" "q-20960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "552d4b9169c04e371eca500ca7fbe5218107176353f77d73bfc1d792861875ab"} {"question" "q-20960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/