.json" "file_sha256" "a1b1558e78f139448bd7d3dc0604a2d5dc146e318d0a8242daebc4b54abd2e9b"} {"question" "e-4699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/49ca24beba2af93482e8e08a7edd396a2714b17f84decd26199741c728ab1bfa.png)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/71e9e1302c0aea79de3370541f0c25acb679e37a5527c172c9490693a4f74c30.png)\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/example-4699.json" "file_sha256" "a1b1558e78f139448bd7d3dc0604a2d5dc146e318d0a8242daebc4b54abd2e9b"} {"question" "e-4700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/13df05563b5770bd877481f24da1c69874d73594e6b82230a2159f01367ba030.png)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/example-4700.json" "file_sha256" "37d1d1799676dbc42b6bd5dac60cc132872decc203ad698149bc0bce97ace79f"} {"question" "e-4700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/4aff0484efeeb7e39af2bdb169b6fff07ce8ba9348ff3a4839423bf5c9ead97d.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/assets/8a7e8b15bc463b00d805547aa64079a1474b5a4595555a5664fba7bfdfb7f62c.png)\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072159/example-4700.json" "file_sha256" "37d1d1799676dbc42b6bd5dac60cc132872decc203ad698149bc0bce97ace79f"}] "usage" {"e-4700" [] "q-130923" [] "q-20782" [] "q-20783" [] "e-4699" [] "q-42167" [] "q-73524" []} "basis" 2618 "retractions" [[17592186105525 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix."] [17592186105525 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y=1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=1+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186105526 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=4 \\\\ 4x+10y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system."] [17592186105526 :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{5}{2}y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-8$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-8,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186307554 17592186307555 17592186307556 17592186307557 17592186307558 17592186307561 17592186307562 17592186307563 17592186307564 17592186307565 17592186307568 17592186307569 17592186307570 17592186307571 17592186307572 17592186307608 17592186307609 17592186307610 17592186307611 17592186307612 17592186323236 17592186323237 17592186323238 17592186323239 17592186323240] "immutable_fields" [[17592186307553 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307553 :answer-field/id] [17592186307553 :answer-field/key] [17592186307553 :answer-field/type] [17592186307560 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307560 :answer-field/id] [17592186307560 :answer-field/key] [17592186307560 :answer-field/type] [17592186307567 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307567 :answer-field/id] [17592186307567 :answer-field/key] [17592186307567 :answer-field/type] [17592186307607 :answer-field/correct] [17592186307607 :answer-field/id] [17592186307607 :answer-field/key] [17592186307607 :answer-field/type] [17592186323235 :answer-field/correct] [17592186323235 :answer-field/id] [17592186323235 :answer-field/key] [17592186323235 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
